{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposal by reason of the poor and awkward internal layout of flat&amp;nbsp;1, insufficient and cramped bedroom space for the ground floor bedroom of flat&amp;nbsp;1 and the subdivision of the modest rear amenity area into two small areas &amp;nbsp;would result in a cramped and poor standard of living accommodation to the the detriment of the residential amenities of the&amp;nbsp;future occupiers&amp;nbsp;and would fail to respect the character and appearance of the host and adjacent dwellings, and the pattern of development in the area, to the detriment of the character of the surrounding area, contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (December 2023), Policy D3 D.1, D.7, D.11 and policy D6 of the London Plan (2021), policy CS1 B of the Harrow Core Strategy (2012), Policies DM 1 and DM 26 of the Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013), and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
